% Test cases for the oral appliances policy (oral_appliances.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33611 and per payment condition
% of dmepos.le. A custom fabricated appliance is a purchase: no rental
% month. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a medical
% reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query,
% so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary,
% and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base oral_appliances cases includes these resources:
    oral_appliances.

the knowledge base oral_appliances cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a custom fabricated appliance (E0486): criteria A-D
% and every documentation requirement in the record. E0486 is not on the
% CMS face-to-face list: the order need only reach the supplier before the
% date of service. A prefabricated appliance (E0485) for the same
% beneficiary, claim 2, is never covered.
scenario custom_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for the prefabricated appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the prefabricated appliance is "E0485".
    the prefabricated appliance is furnished to Ann.
    the prefabricated appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    the order for the prefabricated appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    the order for the oral appliance is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the oral appliance is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the oral appliance includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the oral appliance includes order date.
    the order for the oral appliance includes description of the item.
    the order for the oral appliance includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the oral appliance includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the oral appliance was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the oral appliance was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the oral appliance.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A mild apnea (AHI 9, 12 events) with a documented symptom: criterion B2.
scenario mild_with_hypertension is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Ben.
    Ben has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ben had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ben was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ben is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ben is 9.
    the sleep test of Ben recorded 12 events.
    the medical record of Ben documents hypertension.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The clinical evaluation came after the sleep test: criterion A fails.
scenario evaluation_after_test is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    Cy has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Cy had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the sleep test of Cy was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Cy is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Cy is 40.
    the sleep test of Cy recorded 200 events.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% An AHI of 35 on a short recording of 20 events: criterion B1 fails (fewer
% than 30 events); criterion B3 holds on the treating practitioner's finding
% that the beneficiary could not tolerate a PAP device.
scenario ahi_over_30_pap_not_tolerated is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Dee.
    Dee has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Dee had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Dee was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Dee is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Dee is 35.
    the sleep test of Dee recorded 20 events.
    the finding pap device unsuitable about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "removed the CPAP mask within an hour every night of a three month trial, with claustrophobia and skin breakdown at the bridge of the nose".
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same test with nothing recorded about a PAP device: the answer is
% conditional on that finding alone.
scenario ahi_over_30_no_finding is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Dee.
    Dee has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Dee had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Dee was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Dee is home sleep test.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Dee is 35.
    the sleep test of Dee recorded 20 events.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding pap device unsuitable about Dee is established"].

% The Council finds the record shows neither a trial of PAP nor a
% determination that it is contraindicated: criterion B3 fails and no
% judgment is open.
scenario council_pap_finding_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Eve.
    Eve has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Eve had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Eve was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Eve is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Eve is 35.
    the sleep test of Eve recorded 20 events.
    the finding pap device unsuitable about Eve is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the physician's letter states a preference for an oral appliance; the record shows no trial of a PAP device and no determination that its use is contraindicated".
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    rn expects answers [].

% A qualifying test, but the appliance was provided and billed by the DME
% supplier, not a dentist (criterion D), and the home sleep test was run by
% the DME supplier (Policy Article A52512): two independent failures.
scenario supplier_not_dentist is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Fay.
    Fay has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Fay had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Fay was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Fay is home sleep test.
    the sleep test of Fay was performed by the DME supplier.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Fay is 40.
    the sleep test of Fay recorded 200 events.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    rn expects answers [].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy, and the flip adds the missing proof.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the oral appliance.
    the HCPCS code of the oral appliance is "E0486".
    the oral appliance is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ann has a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea.
    Ann had an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-01-10.
    the sleep test of Ann was performed on 2026-01-25.
    the type of the sleep test of Ann is facility polysomnogram.
    the AHI of the sleep test of Ann is 22.
    the sleep test of Ann recorded 140 events.
    the order for the oral appliance was written by the treating practitioner following a review of the report of the sleep test.
    the oral appliance is provided and billed by a licensed dentist.
    the order for the oral appliance is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the oral appliance is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the oral appliance includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the oral appliance includes order date.
    the order for the oral appliance includes description of the item.
    the order for the oral appliance includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the oral appliance includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the oral appliance was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the oral appliance was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the oral appliance"]].
